From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: bound the wait for a committed GSI transaction

Subset of hotdog 0156-hotdog-integrate-validated-runtime-fixes.patch
(drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.[ch] only). See hotdog
docs/evidence/2026-08-18-ipa-ssr-notifier-deadlock.md: an unbounded wait in
the modem SSR notifier left the modem unrecoverable after a crash.

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.c b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.c
index 19531883864ae6a3a3e039b2fc2629103afa5266..fbe796cd8a0a87844efdd087474fbe4f85949175 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.c
@@ -79,6 +79,13 @@ struct gsi_tre {
 };
 
 /* gsi_tre->flags mask values (in CPU byte order) */
+/* How long to wait for a committed transaction to complete.  Command channel
+ * transactions finish in microseconds; this only has to be generous enough to
+ * never expire on a working device, because the alternative is a wait that
+ * never ends.  GSI_CMD_TIMEOUT in gsi.c bounds the generic commands similarly.
+ */
+#define GSI_TRANS_TIMEOUT	1000	/* milliseconds */
+
 #define TRE_FLAGS_CHAIN_FMASK	GENMASK(0, 0)
 #define TRE_FLAGS_IEOT_FMASK	GENMASK(9, 9)
 #define TRE_FLAGS_BEI_FMASK	GENMASK(10, 10)
@@ -619,7 +626,22 @@ void gsi_trans_commit_wait(struct gsi_trans *trans)
 
 	__gsi_trans_commit(trans, true);
 
-	wait_for_completion(&trans->completion);
+	/* Every caller of this is a command channel operation, and some of
+	 * them run from the modem's SSR notifier chain while holding the
+	 * remote processor lock. Waiting there without a bound is fatal: if
+	 * the transaction never completes, the modem can never be restarted
+	 * and any driver unregistering an SSR notifier blocks behind it.
+	 *
+	 * Timing out is safe. We hold a reference of our own here, and the
+	 * GSI completion path holds the one it took when the transaction was
+	 * committed, so dropping ours below never frees a transaction the
+	 * hardware may still complete later.
+	 */
+	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&trans->completion,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(GSI_TRANS_TIMEOUT)))
+		dev_err(trans->gsi->dev,
+			"channel %u: transaction did not complete in %ums\n",
+			trans->channel_id, GSI_TRANS_TIMEOUT);
 
 out_trans_free:
 	gsi_trans_free(trans);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.h b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.h
index c1b3386cbb9d53c8a262cd7864eafda3a3d9b4ba..0886c222d6ebef7de161550ef08861ec7401f30a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi_trans.h
@@ -202,6 +202,10 @@ void gsi_trans_commit(struct gsi_trans *trans, bool ring_db);
  * gsi_trans_commit_wait() - Commit a GSI transaction and wait for it
  *			     to complete
  * @trans:	Transaction to commit
+ *
+ * The wait is bounded.  If the transaction does not complete in time an error
+ * is logged and the caller continues; callers run from contexts, such as the
+ * modem's SSR notifier chain, where blocking forever wedges the system.
  */
 void gsi_trans_commit_wait(struct gsi_trans *trans);
 
